# Images scripts/check-image-digests.sh may find without a digest. One exact
# reference per line, or `repo:*` for any tag of that repo; "#" starts a
# comment.
#
# Permanent: the system-upgrade-controller derives this image's tag from the
# Plan's `version` field at run time, so the manifest cannot carry one.
rancher/k3s-upgrade

# Permanent: lives in the vendored upstream controller.yaml, which the
# kustomization keeps byte-for-byte so a re-vendor is an overwrite. A digest
# patch over it would silently outlive the next re-vendor. Renovate tracks the
# tag in the vendored file directly, so the entry matches any tag -- an exact
# one failed CI on every release Renovate bumped.
rancher/system-upgrade-controller:*
